# ⚡ Quick Reference (80% de tareas comunes)

| Tarea | Acción Rápida |
|-------|---------------|
| 🔍 Crear feature nueva | Leer: `structure/01-proyecto/` → `03-database/` → `06-componentes/wireframes/` |
| 🛣️ Crear API route | Patrón: RLS Bypass (línea 200) + `structure/07-integraciones/api-routes.md` |
| 🎨 Nuevo componente | Verificar: `structure/06-componentes/wireframes/` + usar primitivos de `ui/` |
| 🗄️ Modificar BD | Verificar PRIMERO: `structure/03-database/schema-completo-enero-26.txt` |
| 🧮 Calcular notas | Leer: `structure/03-database/calculo-notas.md` + usar `lib/grades.ts` |
| 📅 Formatear fechas | Usar: `formatDate()` de `lib/format.ts` (línea 37) |
| 🏷️ Badges de estado | Usar: `<Badge color={getGradeBadge(nota).color}>` |
| 🔐 Verificar auth | Patrón: `verifyAdminOrEditor()` (línea 220) |

📖 Para detalles completos, continúa leyendo las secciones abajo.

# General Behavior & Mindset
- **Act as:** Senior Full Stack Engineer (Next.js + Supabase Expert) in January 2026.
- **Goal:** Scalable, maintainable, and secure code. NO "quick fixes" or "patches". Always solve the root cause.
- **Docs Strategy:** Before implementing, if you are unsure about a library version or API change, explicitly ask permission to search online or check the official docs.
- **Dependency Check:** Always read `package.json` before suggesting new packages. Use existing libraries whenever possible.

# Tech Stack Standards (2026)
- **Framework:** Next.js 16 (App Router). Use Server Components (RSC) by default.
- **State Management:** 
  - Hierarchy: URL state > Server State (React Query) > Local State > Global State (Zustand)
  - React Query: For all server data fetching and mutations
  - Zustand: Only for complex cross-component state (avoid if possible)
- **Backend & Mutations:** 
  - Supabase (PostgreSQL) for database
  - **IMPORTANT:** Use API Routes (`src/app/api/`) + React Query mutations for data modifications
  - **WHY:** Avoids infinite recursion in RLS policies when querying `users` table
  - Server Actions: Only for simple auth operations (see `src/app/actions/auth.ts`)
- **Security:** Sanitize all inputs. Use Zod for validation. Ensure RLS policies are active.

# 🎨 UI & Design System Rules

## Color System - VT (Vue Theme) Palette
- **Source of Truth:** `tailwind.config.ts` lines 56-123 contains official Vue Theme colors
- **Primary palette:** `vt-green`, `vt-blue`, `vt-yellow`, `vt-red`, `vt-purple`
- **Neutrals:** `vt-white`, `vt-black`, `vt-gray-{light|dark}-{1-5}`, `vt-indigo`
- **Semantic colors:** `background`, `foreground`, `primary`, `secondary`, `muted`, `accent`, `destructive`, `border`, `card`, `popover` (use CSS variables via `hsl(var(--primary))`)
- **Usage Rules:**
  - ✅ ALWAYS use VT color classes: `bg-vt-green`, `text-vt-blue-light`, `border-vt-red`
  - ✅ For semantic UI: `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`
  - ❌ NEVER add arbitrary hex codes in component files (e.g., `bg-[#42b883]`)
  - ❌ NEVER use inline styles with colors
- **If color missing:** Extend `tailwind.config.ts` `theme.extend.colors` section, don't hardcode in components

## Components
- **Before creating:** Check if similar component exists in `src/components/`
- **Badge component:** Use `<Badge color="green" colorStyle="soft">` from `ui/badge.tsx`
  - Available colors: green, blue, yellow, red, purple, gray
  - Available styles: solid, soft (default), outline
  - Helper: `getGradeBadge(nota)` from `lib/grades.ts` returns `{ label, color }`
- **Reusability:** Extract reusable logic into generic components with props
- **DRY Principle:** If logic appears twice, abstract to hook (`src/hooks/`) or utility (`src/lib/`)

## Responsive Design
- **Mobile First:** Start with mobile layout, add breakpoints with `md:`, `lg:` as needed
- **Grid layouts:** Force single column on mobile (see `DashboardGrid.tsx` for reference)
- **Testing:** Always verify mobile layout before considering a UI task complete

